  "id": "Compound::DB00349 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Clobazam is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the cytochrome P450 2c18 enzyme. The evidence suggests that Clobazam binds to Cyp2c18, which in turn participates in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities, both of which are catalyzed by Cyp2c19. This creates a chain of enzymatic interactions that may influence the expression or activity of Cyp2c19. Additionally, Clobazam is classified as an inhibitor of Cytochrome P450 2d6, which includes Amiodarone, a compound that directly binds to Cyp2c19. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Clobazam may modulate Cyp2c19 activity, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Clobazam and Cyp2c19, particularly through the indirect influence of Cyp2c18 and its participation in the enzymatic processes of Cyp2c19.",
